  "main_text": "<think>\nOkay, the user is Noah Ito with user ID noah_ito_3850. They want to check the amount they paid for their most recent order. First, I need to get their user details to see their order history.\n\nI should call get_user_details with their user ID. That will list all their orders. Once I have the orders, I can find the most recent one based on the date. Then, I need to get the details of that specific order using get_order_details to find out the total amount paid.\n\nWait, the user mentioned they're not sure how long ago the order was placed, so I need to make sure I identify the latest order correctly. Let me start by retrieving all their orders through get_user_details. Once I have the list, I can sort them by date and pick the newest one. Then, check the payment details from that order. I should present the total amount they paid, including any payment method used. If there's a need for more details, I can provide that too.\n</think>\n\n<tool_call>\n{\"name\": \"get_user_details\", \"arguments\": {\"user_id\": \"noah_ito_3850\"}}\n",
